From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: CMS encapsulated content in signed messages

crypt32: CMS encapsulated content in signed messages

CMSG_CMS_ENCAPSULATED_CONTENT_FLAG makes the signed-message encoder wrap
content whose type is not data in an OCTET STRING and write SignedData version
3; the decoder unwraps it for CMSG_CONTENT_PARAM and for the digest.
CryptSignMessage honours CRYPT_MESSAGE_ENCAPSULATED_CONTENT_OUT_FLAG and
dwInnerContentType, and CryptMsgSignCTL / CryptMsgEncodeAndSignCTL accept
CMSG_CMS_ENCAPSULATED_CTL_FLAG.
